From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyDevices <pydevices@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: the USB host library from the component registry on
 the ESP32-P4 and S31.

ESP-IDF 6 moved the USB host library (usb_host) out of ESP-IDF and into
the component registry as espressif/usb, so a user C module that hosts
USB devices on the ESP32-S31 finds it only there. The ESP32-P4, on
ESP-IDF 5.5, used ESP-IDF's own copy. The port's component manifest now
names espressif/usb 1.6.1 for both high-speed chips; on ESP-IDF 5.5.3 and
later the component replaces ESP-IDF's copy (it brings that copy's PHY
driver along), so the two chips run the same host library and the same
fixes. 1.4.0 added the S31, 1.6.0 lets its controller's DMA reach PSRAM,
and 1.6.1 fixes asserts when a device or a hub is unplugged during a
transfer. The full-speed ESP32-S2 and S3 keep ESP-IDF's copy. Nothing
links it unless a module uses it.
---
 ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml b/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
--- a/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
+++ b/ports/esp32/main/idf_component.yml
@@ -1,4 +1,15 @@
 dependencies:
+  # The USB host library, for a user C module that drives USB devices, on
+  # the two chips whose host controller runs at high speed. From ESP-IDF 6
+  # it is this component and no longer part of ESP-IDF; on ESP-IDF 5.x it
+  # replaces ESP-IDF's own copy, so both chips run the same library. 1.6.0
+  # is the first to take the ESP32-S31's DMA from PSRAM; 1.6.1 fixes asserts
+  # on a device or hub unplugged mid-transfer. The full-speed ESP32-S2 and
+  # S3 keep ESP-IDF's copy. Nothing links it unless a module uses it.
+  espressif/usb:
+    version: "1.6.1"
+    rules:
+      - if: "target in [esp32p4, esp32s31]"
   # holding off on updating mdns as newer versions have higher
   # resource usage
   espressif/mdns: "~1.3.0"
-- 
2.43.0

